{"content":[{"c":["SHEMAIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Prophet during the reign of Rehoboam, king of Judah (930–913 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). He warned the king not to go to war against Jeroboam and the ten northern tribes of Israel (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.12.22-24","r":"1Kgs.12.22-24","rawR":"1Kgs.12.22-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.12.22-24","value":"1Kgs.12.22-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 12:22-24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.2-4","r":"2Chr.11.2-4","rawR":"2Chr.11.2-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.2-4","value":"2Chr.11.2-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:2-4"},"). Five years later he spoke words of comfort to a repentant Rehoboam and people of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.12.5-7","r":"2Chr.12.5-7","rawR":"2Chr.12.5-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.12.5-7","value":"2Chr.12.5-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 12:5-7"},"). Shemaiah chronicled the life of Rehoboam in a book that has since been lost."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Son of Shecaniah, the father of six sons and a descendant of David through Rehoboam’s line (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.22","r":"1Chr.3.22","rawR":"1Chr.3.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.22","value":"1Chr.3.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Simeonite, father of Shimri and an ancestor of Jehu (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.37","r":"1Chr.4.37","rawR":"1Chr.4.37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.37","value":"1Chr.4.37"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:37"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Reubenite and a son of Joel (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.4","r":"1Chr.5.4","rawR":"1Chr.5.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.4","value":"1Chr.5.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:4"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Levite and the son of Hasshub, who returned to Jerusalem after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.14","r":"1Chr.9.14","rawR":"1Chr.9.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.14","value":"1Chr.9.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:14"},"). He was made a leader in the work of the temple during the days of Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.15","r":"Neh.11.15","rawR":"Neh.11.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.15","value":"Neh.11.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6. Son of Galal and the father of Obadiah, a Levite who returned to Jerusalem following the Babylonian captivity (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.16","r":"1Chr.9.16","rawR":"1Chr.9.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.16","value":"1Chr.9.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:16"},"); called Shammua in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.17","r":"Neh.11.17","rawR":"Neh.11.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.17","value":"Neh.11.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 11:17"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 7. Levite and the leader of his father’s house. Shemaiah was summoned by David to help carry the ark from Obed-edom’s house to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.8-11","r":"1Chr.15.8-11","rawR":"1Chr.15.8-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.8-11","value":"1Chr.15.8-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:8-11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 8. Son of Nethanel and the Levitical scribe who recorded the 24 divisions of the priests during David’s reign in Israel (1000–961 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.6","r":"1Chr.24.6","rawR":"1Chr.24.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.6","value":"1Chr.24.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 9. Oldest of Obed-edom’s eight sons and the father of sons who served as the gatekeepers of the south gate and storehouse of the sanctuary during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.26.4-7","r":"1Chr.26.4-7","rawR":"1Chr.26.4-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.26.4-7","value":"1Chr.26.4-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 26:4-7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the Levites sent by King Jehoshaphat of Judah (872–848 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") to teach the law in the cities of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.8-9","r":"2Chr.17.8-9","rawR":"2Chr.17.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.8-9","value":"2Chr.17.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:8-9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Son of Jeduthun and Uzziel’s brother, who was among the Levites chosen by King Hezekiah of Judah (715–686 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") to cleanse the house of the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.14-15","r":"2Chr.29.14-15","rawR":"2Chr.29.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.14-15","value":"2Chr.29.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:14-15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["12. One of the Levites assisting Kore with the distribution of the offerings among his fellow priests living in the priestly cities of Judah during the days of King Hezekiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.31.15","r":"2Chr.31.15","rawR":"2Chr.31.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.31.15","value":"2Chr.31.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 31:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["13. One of the Levitical leaders who generously gave animals to the Levites for the celebration of the Passover feast during King Josiah’s reign (640–609 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.35.9","r":"2Chr.35.9","rawR":"2Chr.35.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.35.9","value":"2Chr.35.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 35:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["14. Son of Adonikam, who returned with Ezra to Judah after the exile during the reign of King Artaxerxes I of Persia (464–424 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.13","r":"Ezra.8.13","rawR":"Ezra.8.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.13","value":"Ezra.8.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["15. One of the Jewish leaders whom Ezra sent to Iddo at Casiphia to gather Levites and temple servants for the caravan of Jews returning to Palestine from Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.16-17","r":"Ezra.8.16-17","rawR":"Ezra.8.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.16-17","value":"Ezra.8.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:16-17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["16. Priest and one of Harim’s five sons who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.21","r":"Ezra.10.21","rawR":"Ezra.10.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.21","value":"Ezra.10.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["17. Son of another Harim who was encouraged by Ezra to divorce his foreign wife (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.31","r":"Ezra.10.31","rawR":"Ezra.10.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.31","value":"Ezra.10.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:31"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["18. Son of Shecaniah and the keeper of the East Gate who repaired a section of the Jerusalem wall under Nehemiah’s direction (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.29","r":"Neh.3.29","rawR":"Neh.3.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.29","value":"Neh.3.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["19. Son of Delaiah and a false prophet hired by Tobiah and Sanballat to frighten Nehemiah and hinder him from rebuilding the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.6.10-13","r":"Neh.6.10-13","rawR":"Neh.6.10-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.6.10-13","value":"Neh.6.10-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 6:10-13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["20. One of the priests who set his seal on the covenant of Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.8","r":"Neh.10.8","rawR":"Neh.10.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.8","value":"Neh.10.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["21. One of the leaders of the priests who returned with Zerubbabel and Jeshua to Judah after the exile (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.6","r":"Neh.12.6","rawR":"Neh.12.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.6","value":"Neh.12.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["22. One of the princes of Judah who participated in the dedication of the Jerusalem wall during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.34","r":"Neh.12.34","rawR":"Neh.12.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.34","value":"Neh.12.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["23. Son of Mattaniah, grandfather of Zechariah, and a descendant of Asaph. Zechariah was one of the priests who played a trumpet at the dedication of the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.35","r":"Neh.12.35","rawR":"Neh.12.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.35","value":"Neh.12.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["24–25. Two priestly musicians who performed at the dedication of the Jerusalem wall (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.36,42","r":"Neh.12.36,42","rawR":"Neh.12.36,42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.36,42","value":"Neh.12.36,42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:36, 42"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["26. Father of Uriah the prophet from Kiriath-jearim. Like Jeremiah, his contemporary, Uriah spoke words of doom against Jerusalem and Judah during the reign of King Jehoiakim of Judah (609–598 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), who deplored Uriah’s message and eventually had him killed (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.26.20-21","r":"Jer.26.20-21","rawR":"Jer.26.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.26.20-21","value":"Jer.26.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 26:20-21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["27. Nehelamite and a Jew deported to Babylon by Nebuchadnezzar, from where he opposed Jeremiah. He sent letters to the priests in Jerusalem that criticized Jeremiah for predicting a long captivity for Judah. Jeremiah exposed Shemaiah as a false prophet and foretold that he and his descendants would not live to see the return to Palestine (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.29.24-32","r":"Jer.29.24-32","rawR":"Jer.29.24-32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.29.24-32","value":"Jer.29.24-32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 29:24-32"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["28. Father of Delaiah, a prince of Judah during the reign of King Jehoiakim (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.12","r":"Jer.36.12","rawR":"Jer.36.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.12","value":"Jer.36.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["29. A kinsman of Tobit (",{"href":"?bref=Tb.5.14","r":"Tb.5.14","rawR":"Tb.5.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Tb.5.14","value":"Tb.5.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Tb 5:14"},"); also spelled Shemeliah."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shemaiah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 12:22-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.12.22-24","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.12.22-24","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.12.22-24"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:2-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.2-4","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.2-4","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.2-4"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 12:5-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.12.5-7","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.12.5-7","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.12.5-7"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.22","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.22","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.37","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.37","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.37"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.4"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.14","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.14","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.14"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.15","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.15","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.16","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.16","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.16"},{"anchorText":"Nehemiah 11:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.17","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.17","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:8-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.8-11","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.8-11","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.8-11"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 24:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.24.6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.24.6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.24.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 26:4-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.26.4-7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.26.4-7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.26.4-7"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 17:8-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.17.8-9","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.17.8-9","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.17.8-9"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 29:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.29.14-15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.29.14-15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.29.14-15"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 31:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.31.15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.31.15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.31.15"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 35:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.35.9","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.35.9","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.35.9"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.13","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.13","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.13"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:16-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.16-17","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.16-17","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.16-17"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.21","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.21","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.21"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.31","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.31","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.31"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.29","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.29","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.29"},{"anchorText":"Neh 6:10-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.6.10-13","rawQueryValue":"Neh.6.10-13","sourceRefExact":"Neh.6.10-13"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.8","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.8","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.8"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.6","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.6","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.6"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.34","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.34","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.34"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.35","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.35","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.35"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:36, 42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.36,42","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.36,42","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.36,42"},{"anchorText":"Jer 26:20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.26.20-21","rawQueryValue":"Jer.26.20-21","sourceRefExact":"Jer.26.20-21"},{"anchorText":"Jer 29:24-32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.29.24-32","rawQueryValue":"Jer.29.24-32","sourceRefExact":"Jer.29.24-32"},{"anchorText":"Jer 36:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.12","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.12","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.12"},{"anchorText":"Tb 5:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Tb.5.14","rawQueryValue":"Tb.5.14","sourceRefExact":"Tb.5.14"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e844b933224a29e9cc9a05712c7f8aec9c5b48e0fa5edd484323609c472b51ca","sourceItemName":"Shemaiah","sourceItemOrder":273,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shemaiah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shemaiah","title":"Shemaiah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}